# T_SCRR: backup.  An empty directory sends nothing; a
# directory that does not exist is refused (200 naming DIR, the
# client's text); a bad name is refused with the server's text (102);
# then the backup to BAK succeeds (the test's answer).  The requests
# are checked by T_SCRR.
S DIRQ
K ENTER ESC
T nosuch
K ENTER
S NODIR
K ESC
T a*b
K ENTER
S BADNAME
K ESC
T bak
K ENTER
S BACKEDUP
K ESC
